<title>BRAZIL: Brazil panel to vote on petroleum bill Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Brazil panel to vote on petroleum bill Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A committee in Brazil's Chamber of Deputies was due to vote Wednesday on a bill regulating the opening up of the country's petroleum monopoly, a congressional official said.</p>
<p>The official said a special lower house panel was scheduled to meet at 1000 local/1300 GMT to vote on the bill which would allow private companies to compete with state-owned Petrobras or go into partnership with it.</p>
<p>If approved in the committee vote, the bill advances to the floor of the lower house. It also has to be approved in the Senate.</p>
<p>(( --William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
